1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,500
Speaker 0: Good morning, everyone.

2
00:00:02,580 --> 00:00:04,740
Speaker 0: Thanks for making it on short notice.

3
00:00:05,820 --> 00:00:08,140
Speaker 0: We have four items on the agenda today.

4
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:12,800
Speaker 0: Let's get started with the new elective proposal from Ramesh.

5
00:00:14,420 --> 00:00:15,300
Speaker 2: Thank you, ma'am.

6
00:00:16,379 --> 00:00:20,220
Speaker 2: So, I've drafted the syllabus for Applied Deep Learning.

7
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:24,700
Speaker 2: The course code will be UE24AM350A.

8
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:28,740
Speaker 2: I'm proposing it as a sixth semester elective.

9
00:00:29,080 --> 00:00:31,420
Speaker 2: with machine learning as the prerequisite.

10
00:00:33,020 --> 00:00:34,500
Speaker 3: Ramesh, quick question.

11
00:00:35,540 --> 00:00:38,140
Speaker 3: How does this overlap with my NLP course?

12
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:40,840
Speaker 3: We both cover transformers.

13
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:43,940
Speaker 2: That's a fair concern.

14
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:46,800
Speaker 2: I was thinking we could split it.

15
00:00:47,880 --> 00:00:51,480
Speaker 2: I'll focus on vision transformers and image generation.

16
00:00:52,480 --> 00:00:54,560
Speaker 2: You keep the language modeling side.

17
00:00:55,520 --> 00:00:56,320
Speaker 2: Would that work?

18
00:00:57,980 --> 00:00:59,040
Speaker 3: Yes, that works.

19
00:01:00,140 --> 00:01:05,379
Speaker 3: I'll update my syllabus to remove the vision parts and expand on attention mechanisms instead.

20
00:01:07,100 --> 00:01:07,320
Speaker 0: Good.

21
00:01:08,440 --> 00:01:09,240
Speaker 0: That's settled.

22
00:01:10,340 --> 00:01:14,400
Speaker 0: Ramesh, when can you submit the final syllabus to the board of studies?

23
00:01:16,160 --> 00:01:18,460
Speaker 2: I can have it ready by next Friday.

24
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:20,560
Speaker 0: Perfect.

25
00:01:21,680 --> 00:01:22,360
Speaker 0: Next item.

26
00:01:23,460 --> 00:01:25,120
Speaker 0: Pavan, the lab situation.

27
00:01:26,820 --> 00:01:29,560
Speaker 1: So we have 8 workstations in AI lab 2.

28
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:31,760
Speaker 1: Only 4 have GPUs.

29
00:01:32,840 --> 00:01:36,580
Speaker 1: For the new elective, we'll need at least 4 more GPU-enabled machines.

30
00:01:37,700 --> 00:01:39,240
Speaker 1: I got quotes from 3 vendors.

31
00:01:40,260 --> 00:01:43,280
Speaker 1: The best one is Dell at 75,000 per workstation.

32
00:01:44,360 --> 00:01:46,580
Speaker 1: So about 3 lakhs total for the upgrade.

33
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:48,880
Speaker 0: 3 lakhs?

34
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,600
Speaker 0: Can we get this approved in this financial year?

35
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:56,120
Speaker 1: If we submit by month-end, yes.

36
00:01:57,180 --> 00:01:59,700
Speaker 1: The administration needs 2 weeks for processing.

37
00:02:01,420 --> 00:02:01,720
Speaker 0: Okay.

38
00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:04,980
Speaker 0: Pavan, you coordinate with purchase.

39
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:08,280
Speaker 0: Get the PO raised by the 25th.

40
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:14,120
Speaker 0: Ramesh, since this is for your course, work with Pawan on the specifications.

41
00:02:15,760 --> 00:02:16,080
Speaker 2: Will do.

42
00:02:18,080 --> 00:02:18,740
Speaker 0: Third item.

43
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:22,780
Speaker 0: Student complains about the capstone workload.

44
00:02:23,940 --> 00:02:28,360
Speaker 0: I've received emails from four teams saying the phase one deadline is too tight.

45
00:02:29,460 --> 00:02:29,840
Speaker 0: Thoughts?

46
00:02:31,560 --> 00:02:32,980
Speaker 3: I've heard similar concerns.

47
00:02:34,040 --> 00:02:38,240
Speaker 3: The 12-week timeline assumes teams already have their topics finalized.

48
00:02:38,640 --> 00:02:40,120
Speaker 3: which isn't always the case.

49
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:44,160
Speaker 2: What if we extended it to 14 weeks?

50
00:02:45,140 --> 00:02:48,820
Speaker 2: That gives them to more weeks for the literature survey phase.

51
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:51,440
Speaker 0: That's reasonable.

52
00:02:52,540 --> 00:02:53,500
Speaker 0: Any objections?

53
00:02:54,660 --> 00:02:54,740
Speaker 0: No?

54
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,040
Speaker 0: Then it's decided.

55
00:02:58,160 --> 00:02:59,980
Speaker 0: Phase 1 is now 14 weeks.

56
00:03:01,140 --> 00:03:02,120
Speaker 0: I'll notify Dr.

57
00:03:02,200 --> 00:03:06,940
Speaker 0: Tetna who handles the capstone coordination and she can update the handbook.

58
00:03:08,600 --> 00:03:10,380
Speaker 1: What about teens already in progress?

59
00:03:11,420 --> 00:03:13,200
Speaker 1: Does this apply to them retroactively?

60
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:15,580
Speaker 0: Good point.

61
00:03:16,740 --> 00:03:19,080
Speaker 0: Yes, current teams get the extension.

62
00:03:20,220 --> 00:03:24,000
Speaker 0: Their new deadline is December 22nd instead of December 8th.

63
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:28,220
Speaker 3: I'll announce this in my Phase 1 class tomorrow.

64
00:03:30,020 --> 00:03:30,420
Speaker 0: Thank you.

65
00:03:31,640 --> 00:03:32,320
Speaker 0: Last item.

66
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:37,200
Speaker 0: The TCS Campus recruitment is confirmed for January 8th.

67
00:03:38,300 --> 00:03:40,240
Speaker 0: Pavan, you're handling logistics?

68
00:03:41,920 --> 00:03:42,220
Speaker 1: Yes.

69
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:45,060
Speaker 1: Booking the seminar hall is done.

70
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:48,600
Speaker 1: Online assessment will use the new computer lab.

71
00:03:49,660 --> 00:03:51,260
Speaker 1: We need about 200 seats.

72
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:54,260
Speaker 1: I'm coordinating with the placement cell.

73
00:03:55,920 --> 00:03:58,320
Speaker 2: Are we running mock interviews beforehand?

74
00:03:59,900 --> 00:04:01,000
Speaker 1: Planning two sessions.

75
00:04:02,140 --> 00:04:04,800
Speaker 1: One on December 20 for aptitude and technical.

76
00:04:05,880 --> 00:04:08,580
Speaker 1: Another on December 27 for HR rounds.

77
00:04:09,660 --> 00:04:12,400
Speaker 1: Both sessions are mandatory for students who registered.

78
00:04:14,100 --> 00:04:14,320
Speaker 0: Good.

79
00:04:15,440 --> 00:04:19,220
Speaker 0: Make sure the mentor assignments are finalized by next week.

80
00:04:20,339 --> 00:04:22,420
Speaker 0: Ramesh, your mentoring batch, eh?

81
00:04:24,080 --> 00:04:24,300
Speaker 2: Yes.

82
00:04:24,320 --> 00:04:26,140
Speaker 2: 12 students.

83
00:04:27,220 --> 00:04:29,000
Speaker 2: I've already met them once.

84
00:04:30,660 --> 00:04:31,160
Speaker 0: Excellent.

85
00:04:32,280 --> 00:04:33,280
Speaker 0: Any other business?

86
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:34,520
Speaker 0: No?

87
00:04:35,780 --> 00:04:36,600
Speaker 0: Then we are done.

88
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:39,040
Speaker 0: Same time next week.

89
00:04:40,120 --> 00:04:42,600
Speaker 0: Thank you everyone.

